Subject: [PATCH] Swift: Skip villager POI searches that cannot find anything

AcquirePoi (bed / job site / meeting point) searches 48 blocks every
20-40 ticks per villager and in trading halls almost never finds
anything. Remember a search that found no candidate at all (the position
predicate, which has side effects, was never called) per behaviour
instance, keyed on world, source block and the sum of per-chunk POI
change counters over the search box (bumped in PoiManager#setDirty, which
every POI add/remove/refresh and ticket change goes through; counters
never decrease). A repeat search from the same block with an unchanged
sum is skipped: same empty result, no side effect skipped. RNG use,
retry-marker cleanup and the path step are untouched.

-Dswift.verify=true still runs every skipped search and reports any that
would have seen a candidate. Disable with -Dswift.poiEmptySearchCache=false.

Hall of 30 wandering villagers, 400 ticks: 1353 searches -> 597 run,
724 skipped.

